{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-169099" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074346/assets/f437bd795c0ccf57a45299bd5f2ff2ac79c5f6bee599183cf7f7463c34fb3edb.png)\n\nThe thin rectangular plate shown above has the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)=2x{y}^{2}.$\n\nCurrent part:\n\nFind the total mass $M$ of the plate.\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $M\\,=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074346/state.json" "file_sha256" "db42fae141462cbd1a73d50910caa065481c7b07f74f1263cc5cff28557bb396"} {"question" "q-169099" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The mass $M$ of a plate that occupies the region \n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 3,\\,0\\le y\\le 2}\n$$\n\nwith mass density $\\lambda (x,y)=2x{y}^{2}$ is given by\n\n$$\nM={∬}_{D}2x{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nFirst, we express our double integral as a repeated integral:      \n \n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}2x{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A={\\int }_{0}^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{3}2x{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y\n$$\n\nNow, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $x$, treating $y$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{3}2x{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{y}^{2}[{\\int }_{0}^{3}2x\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{y}^{2}[{x}^{2}]_{x=0}^{x=3}\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{y}^{2}({3}^{2}-0)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}9{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we integrate with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}9{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y & =[3{y}^{3}]_{y=0}^{y=2} \\\\  & =3({2}^{3}-0) \\\\  & =24\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the mass of the plate is $M=24.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074346/state.json" "file_sha256" "db42fae141462cbd1a73d50910caa065481c7b07f74f1263cc5cff28557bb396"} {"question" "q-169099" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074346/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f385f37b318df1aaf5bf9a6af6ed211508f4f695eb694b50cea9e32ff10a47f0"} {"question" "q-169099" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074346/state.json" "file_sha256" "db42fae141462cbd1a73d50910caa065481c7b07f74f1263cc5cff28557bb396"} {"question" "q-169099" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "24"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074346/state.json" "file_sha256" "db42fae141462cbd1a73d50910caa065481c7b07f74f1263cc5cff28557bb396"} {"question" "q-169100" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074346/assets/f437bd795c0ccf57a45299bd5f2ff2ac79c5f6bee599183cf7f7463c34fb3edb.png)\n\nThe thin rectangular plate shown above has the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)=2x{y}^{2}.$\n\nEarlier part 1:\n\nFind the total mass $M$ of the plate.\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $M\\,=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $24$\n\nCurrent part:\n\nFind the moment ${M}_{x}$ of the plate about the $x$-axis.\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${M}_{x}\\,=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074346/state.json" "file_sha256" "db42fae141462cbd1a73d50910caa065481c7b07f74f1263cc5cff28557bb396"} {"question" "q-169100" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The moment of a lamina $D$ with the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)$ about the $x$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{M}_{x}={∬}_{D}y\\,\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $\\lambda (x,y)=2x{y}^{2}$ and the plate occupies the region\n\n$$\nD={(x,y):0\\le x\\le 3,\\,0\\le y\\le 2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{x} & ={∬}_{D}y\\cdot 2x{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}2x{y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{3}2x{y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{y}^{3}{[{x}^{2}]}_{x=0}^{x=3}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{y}^{3}({3}^{2}-0)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}9{y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={[\\frac{9}{4}{y}^{4}]}_{y=0}^{y=2} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{4}(2)^{4}-0 \\\\  & =36.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074346/state.json" "file_sha256" "db42fae141462cbd1a73d50910caa065481c7b07f74f1263cc5cff28557bb396"} {"question" "q-169100" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074346/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f385f37b318df1aaf5bf9a6af6ed211508f4f695eb694b50cea9e32ff10a47f0"} {"question" "q-169100" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074346/state.json" "file_sha256" "db42fae141462cbd1a73d50910caa065481c7b07f74f1263cc5cff28557bb396"} {"question" "q-169100" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "36"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074346/state.json" "file_sha256" "db42fae141462cbd1a73d50910caa065481c7b07f74f1263cc5cff28557bb396"} {"question" "q-169101" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074346/assets/f437bd795c0ccf57a45299bd5f2ff2ac79c5f6bee599183cf7f7463c34fb3edb.png)\n\nThe thin rectangular plate shown above has the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)=2x{y}^{2}.$\n\nEarlier part 1:\n\nFind the total mass $M$ of the plate.\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $M\\,=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $24$\n\nEarlier part 2:\n\nFind the moment ${M}_{x}$ of the plate about the $x$-axis.\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${M}_{x}\\,=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $36$\n\nCurrent part:\n\nFind the moment ${M}_{y}$ of the plate about the $y$-axis.\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${M}_{y}\\,=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074346/state.json" "file_sha256" "db42fae141462cbd1a73d50910caa065481c7b07f74f1263cc5cff28557bb396"} {"question" "q-169101" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The moment of a lamina $D$ with the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)$ about the $y$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{M}_{y}={∬}_{D}x\\,\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nIn our case, $\\lambda (x,y)=2x{y}^{2}$ and the plate occupies the region\n\n$$\nD={(x,y):0\\le x\\le 3,\\,0\\le y\\le 2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{y} & ={∬}_{D}x\\cdot 2x{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}2{x}^{2}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2}2{x}^{2}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}2{x}^{2}{[\\frac{1}{3}{y}^{3}]}_{y=0}^{y=2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}2{x}^{2}(\\frac{8}{3}-0)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{16}{3}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{16{x}^{3}}{9}]}_{x=0}^{x=3} \\\\  & =\\frac{16(3)^{3}}{9}-0 \\\\  & =48.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074346/state.json" "file_sha256" "db42fae141462cbd1a73d50910caa065481c7b07f74f1263cc5cff28557bb396"} {"question" "q-169101" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074346/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f385f37b318df1aaf5bf9a6af6ed211508f4f695eb694b50cea9e32ff10a47f0"} {"question" "q-169101" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074346/state.json" "file_sha256" "db42fae141462cbd1a73d50910caa065481c7b07f74f1263cc5cff28557bb396"} {"question" "q-169101" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "48"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074346/state.json" "file_sha256" "db42fae141462cbd1a73d50910caa065481c7b07f74f1263cc5cff28557bb396"} {"question" "q-169102" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074346/assets/f437bd795c0ccf57a45299bd5f2ff2ac79c5f6bee599183cf7f7463c34fb3edb.png)\n\nThe thin rectangular plate shown above has the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)=2x{y}^{2}.$\n\nEarlier part 1:\n\nFind the total mass $M$ of the plate.\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $M\\,=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $24$\n\nEarlier part 2:\n\nFind the moment ${M}_{x}$ of the plate about the $x$-axis.\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${M}_{x}\\,=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $36$\n\nEarlier part 3:\n\nFind the moment ${M}_{y}$ of the plate about the $y$-axis.\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${M}_{y}\\,=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $48$\n\nCurrent part:\n\nFind the coordinates of the center of mass of the plate.\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $(\\overset{―}{x},\\overset{―}{y})=($\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                         \n$,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-2}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$)$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074346/state.json" "file_sha256" "db42fae141462cbd1a73d50910caa065481c7b07f74f1263cc5cff28557bb396"} {"question" "q-169102" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The center of mass of a lamina $D$ with the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)$ is given by \n\n$$\n(\\overset{―}{x},\\overset{―}{y})=(\\frac{{M}_{y}}{M},\\frac{{M}_{x}}{M}),\n$$\n\nwhere \n\n* $M={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A$ is the mass of the lamina,\n\n* ${M}_{x}={∬}_{D}y\\,\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A\\,$ is the moment of the lamina about the $x$-axis, and\n\n* ${M}_{y}={∬}_{D}x\\,\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A$ is the moment of the lamina about the $y$-axis.\n\nIn part 1, we found that the mass of the plate is\n\n$$\nM=24.\n$$\n\nAlso, from parts 2 and 3, we know that \n\n$$\n{M}_{x}=36,\\,{M}_{y}=48.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{x}=\\frac{{M}_{y}}{M}=\\frac{48}{24}=2,\\,\\,\\overset{―}{y}=\\frac{{M}_{x}}{M}=\\frac{36}{24}=\\frac{3}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the center of mass of the lamina is $(2,\\frac{3}{2}).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074346/state.json" "file_sha256" "db42fae141462cbd1a73d50910caa065481c7b07f74f1263cc5cff28557bb396"} {"question" "q-169102" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074346/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f385f37b318df1aaf5bf9a6af6ed211508f4f695eb694b50cea9e32ff10a47f0"} {"question" "q-169102" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074346/state.json" "file_sha256" "db42fae141462cbd1a73d50910caa065481c7b07f74f1263cc5cff28557bb396"} {"question" "q-169102" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074346/state.json" "file_sha256" "db42fae141462cbd1a73d50910caa065481c7b07f74f1263cc5cff28557bb396"} {"question" "q-169102" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074346/state.json" "file_sha256" "db42fae141462cbd1a73d50910caa065481c7b07f74f1263cc5cff28557bb396"} {"question" "q-169102" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{3}{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074346/state.json" "file_sha256" "db42fae141462cbd1a73d50910caa065481c7b07f74f1263cc5cff28557bb396"} {"question" "q-169103" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074346/assets/f437bd795c0ccf57a45299bd5f2ff2ac79c5f6bee599183cf7f7463c34fb3edb.png)\n\nThe thin rectangular plate shown above has the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)=2x{y}^{2}.$\n\nEarlier part 1:\n\nFind the total mass $M$ of the plate.\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $M\\,=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $24$\n\nEarlier part 2:\n\nFind the moment ${M}_{x}$ of the plate about the $x$-axis.\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${M}_{x}\\,=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $36$\n\nEarlier part 3:\n\nFind the moment ${M}_{y}$ of the plate about the $y$-axis.\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${M}_{y}\\,=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $48$\n\nEarlier part 4:\n\nFind the coordinates of the center of mass of the plate.\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $(\\overset{―}{x},\\overset{―}{y})=($\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $2$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                         \n$,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $\\frac{3}{2}$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$)$\n\nCurrent part:\n\nFind the moment of inertia ${I}_{y}$ of this plate about the $y$-axis.\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${I}_{y}\\,=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074346/state.json" "file_sha256" "db42fae141462cbd1a73d50910caa065481c7b07f74f1263cc5cff28557bb396"} {"question" "q-169103" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a plane lamina $D$ with mass density function $\\lambda (x,y),$ the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{y}={∬}_{D}{x}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula for ${I}_{y},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{y} & ={∬}_{D}{x}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}{x}^{2}\\cdot 2x{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}2{x}^{3}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{3}2{x}^{3}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}2{y}^{2}{[\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{4}]}_{x=0}^{x=3}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}2{y}^{2}(\\frac{81}{4}-0)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{81}{2}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={[\\frac{27}{2}{y}^{3}]}_{y=0}^{y=2} \\\\  & =\\frac{27}{2}({2}^{3}-0) \\\\  & =108.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074346/state.json" "file_sha256" "db42fae141462cbd1a73d50910caa065481c7b07f74f1263cc5cff28557bb396"} {"question" "q-169103" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074346/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f385f37b318df1aaf5bf9a6af6ed211508f4f695eb694b50cea9e32ff10a47f0"} {"question" "q-169103" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074346/state.json" "file_sha256" "db42fae141462cbd1a73d50910caa065481c7b07f74f1263cc5cff28557bb396"} {"question" "q-169103" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" 