                      \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074346/state.json" "file_sha256" "db42fae141462cbd1a73d50910caa065481c7b07f74f1263cc5cff28557bb396"} {"question" "q-169104" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ with mass $M$ and mass density function $\\lambda (x,y),$ the radius of gyration ${R}_{y}$ about the $y$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{R}_{y}=\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{y}}{M}},\n$$\n\nwhere ${I}_{y}$ is the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis.\n\nIn part 1, we found that the mass of the plate is\n\n$$\nM=24.\n$$\n\nAlso, from part 5, we know that the moment of inertia of the lamina about the $y$-axis is \n\n$$\n{I}_{y}=108.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the radius of gyration about the $y$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{R}_{y} & =\\sqrt{\\frac{{I}_{y}}{M}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{108}{24}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{9}{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074346/state.json" "file_sha256" "db42fae141462cbd1a73d50910caa065481c7b07f74f1263cc5cff28557bb396"} {"question" "q-169104" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074346/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f385f37b318df1aaf5bf9a6af6ed211508f4f695eb694b50cea9e32ff10a47f0"} {"question" "q-169104" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074346/state.json" "file_sha256" "db42fae141462cbd1a73d50910caa065481c7b07f74f1263cc5cff28557bb396"} {"question" "q-169104" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074346/state.json" "file_sha256" "db42fae141462cbd1a73d50910caa065481c7b07f74f1263cc5cff28557bb396"} {"question" "q-169105" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074346/assets/f437bd795c0ccf57a45299bd5f2ff2ac79c5f6bee599183cf7f7463c34fb3edb.png)\n\nThe thin rectangular plate shown above has the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)=2x{y}^{2}.$\n\nEarlier part 1:\n\nFind the total mass $M$ of the plate.\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $M\\,=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $24$\n\nEarlier part 2:\n\nFind the moment ${M}_{x}$ of the plate about the $x$-axis.\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${M}_{x}\\,=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $36$\n\nEarlier part 3:\n\nFind the moment ${M}_{y}$ of the plate about the $y$-axis.\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${M}_{y}\\,=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $48$\n\nEarlier part 4:\n\nFind the coordinates of the center of mass of the plate.\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $(\\overset{―}{x},\\overset{―}{y})=($\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $2$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                         \n$,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $\\frac{3}{2}$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$)$\n\nEarlier part 5:\n\nFind the moment of inertia ${I}_{y}$ of this plate about the $y$-axis.\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${I}_{y}\\,=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $108$\n\nEarlier part 6:\n\nFind the radius of gyration ${R}_{y}$ of the plate about the $y$-axis.\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${R}_{y}\\,=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{2}$\n\nCurrent part:\n\nFind the moment of inertia ${I}_{s}$ of the plate about the line $s$ with equation $y=2.$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${I}_{s}\\,=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074346/state.json" "file_sha256" "db42fae141462cbd1a73d50910caa065481c7b07f74f1263cc5cff28557bb396"} {"question" "q-169105" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The moment of inertia of a plane lamina in the shape of a region $D$ about an axis of rotation $s$ is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{s}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\lambda (x,y)$ is the mass density function of the lamina, and $r(x,y)$ is the distance from the line $l$ to the point $(x,y)$ on $D.$\n\nThe distance between a point $(x,y)$ on $D$ and the line $y=2$ is given by\n\n$$\nr(x,y)=|y-2|.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the line $y=2$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{s} & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (x,y)[r(x,y)]^{2}\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{3}2x{y}^{2}|y-2{|}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{3}2x{y}^{2}(y-2)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{y}^{2}(y-2)^{2}[{x}^{2}]_{x=0}^{x=3}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{y}^{2}({y}^{2}-4y+4)({3}^{2}-0)\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =9{\\int }_{0}^{2}({y}^{4}-4{y}^{3}+4{y}^{2})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =9{[\\frac{{y}^{5}}{5}-{y}^{4}+\\frac{4}{3}{y}^{3}]}_{y=0}^{y=2} \\\\  & =9[\\frac{32}{5}-16+\\frac{32}{3}] \\\\  & =\\frac{48}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074346/state.json" "file_sha256" "db42fae141462cbd1a73d50910caa065481c7b07f74f1263cc5cff28557bb396"} {"question" "q-169105" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074346/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f385f37b318df1aaf5bf9a6af6ed211508f4f695eb694b50cea9e32ff10a47f0"} {"question" "q-169105" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074346/state.json" "file_sha256" "db42fae141462cbd1a73d50910caa065481c7b07f74f1263cc5cff28557bb396"} {"question" "q-169105" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{48}{5}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074346/state.json" "file_sha256" "db42fae141462cbd1a73d50910caa065481c7b07f74f1263cc5cff28557bb396"} {"question" "q-169106" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074346/assets/f437bd795c0ccf57a45299bd5f2ff2ac79c5f6bee599183cf7f7463c34fb3edb.png)\n\nThe thin rectangular plate shown above has the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)=2x{y}^{2}.$\n\nEarlier part 1:\n\nFind the total mass $M$ of the plate.\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $M\\,=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $24$\n\nEarlier part 2:\n\nFind the moment ${M}_{x}$ of the plate about the $x$-axis.\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${M}_{x}\\,=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $36$\n\nEarlier part 3:\n\nFind the moment ${M}_{y}$ of the plate about the $y$-axis.\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${M}_{y}\\,=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $48$\n\nEarlier part 4:\n\nFind the coordinates of the center of mass of the plate.\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $(\\overset{―}{x},\\overset{―}{y})=($\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $2$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                         \n$,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $\\frac{3}{2}$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$)$\n\nEarlier part 5:\n\nFind the moment of inertia ${I}_{y}$ of this plate about the $y$-axis.\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${I}_{y}\\,=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $108$\n\nEarlier part 6:\n\nFind the radius of gyration ${R}_{y}$ of the plate about the $y$-axis.\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${R}_{y}\\,=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{2}$\n\nEarlier part 7:\n\nFind the moment of inertia ${I}_{s}$ of the plate about the line $s$ with equation $y=2.$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${I}_{s}\\,=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $\\frac{48}{5}$\n\nCurrent part:\n\nThe moment of inertia of the plate about the axis perpendicular to the plate passing through its center of mass is ${I}_{M}=\\frac{78}{5}.$ Find the moment of inertia ${I}_{l}$ of the plate about the axis $l$ that is perpendicular to the plate and passes through the point $(1,1).$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${I}_{l}\\,=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074346/state.json" "file_sha256" "db42fae141462cbd1a73d50910caa065481c7b07f74f1263cc5cff28557bb396"} {"question" "q-169106" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "For a plane lamina of mass $M$ and a line ${l}_{M}$ perpendicular to the lamina passing through its center of mass, the parallel axis theorem states that the moment of inertia of the lamina about a line $l$ parallel to ${l}_{M}$ is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{l}={I}_{M}+{d}^{2}M,\n$$\n\nwhere $d$ is the distance between the lines, and ${I}_{M}$ and ${I}_{l}$ are the moments of inertia about the lines ${l}_{M}$ and $l,$ respectively.\n\nIn part 1, we found that the mass of the plate is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M=24.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe squared distance between the line through the center of mass $(2,\\frac{3}{2})$ and the line through the point $(1,1)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{d}^{2} & ={(2-1)}^{2}+{(\\frac{3}{2}-1)}^{2} \\\\  & =1+\\frac{1}{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, applying the parallel axis theorem, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{l} & =\\frac{78}{5}+\\frac{5}{4}\\cdot 24 \\\\  & =\\frac{78}{5}+30 \\\\  & =\\frac{228}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074346/state.json" "file_sha256" "db42fae141462cbd1a73d50910caa065481c7b07f74f1263cc5cff28557bb396"} {"question" "q-169106" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074346/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f385f37b318df1aaf5bf9a6af6ed211508f4f695eb694b50cea9e32ff10a47f0"} {"question" "q-169106" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074346/state.json" "file_sha256" "db42fae141462cbd1a73d50910caa065481c7b07f74f1263cc5cff28557bb396"} {"question" "q-169106" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{228}{5}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14074346/state.json" "file_sha256" "db42fae141462cbd1a73d50910caa065481c7b07f74f1263cc5cff28557bb396"}] "usage" {} "basis" 2725 "retractions" [] "immutable_answers" [] "immutable_fields" [] "no_history" []}
